@node Getting Started
@chapter Getting Started
@cindex getting started

This chapter is a guided tour of @code{beads.el}: it opens the board,
creates a first issue, and explains the interaction patterns every view
shares.  Install the package first (@pxref{Installation and
Requirements}); the vocabulary the rest of the manual assumes is defined
in @ref{Concepts}, and the commands that create, list, view, edit, close,
and label issues are in @ref{Issue Workflow}.

@menu
* Your First Issue::        Open the board and create an issue.
* Interface Concepts::      Modes, transients, actions, movement, stores.
@end menu

@node Your First Issue
@section Your First Issue
@cindex first issue

@deffn Command beads
Open the Beads board for the current project.  This is the primary entry
point of @code{beads.el}; it opens the full board (@code{beads-dashboard}).
Press @kbd{?} inside the buffer for the @code{beads-dispatch} menu.
@end deffn

@enumerate
@item
Open the board: @kbd{M-x beads}.
@item
Press @kbd{?} for the dispatch menu, then @kbd{c} to create an issue.
@item
Type the title on the first line, then the description below it.
@item
Press @kbd{C-c C-c} to submit.  The new issue appears in refreshed lists.
@end enumerate

From the board, press @kbd{?} again and use:

@table @kbd
@item l
List all issues.
@item r
List ready (unblocked) work.
@item b
List blocked work.
@item D
Open the full project dashboard.
@end table

@node Interface Concepts
@section Interface Concepts
